## Part 10 — Component Registration Checklist

When adding a new component, update ALL of these:

1. **CSS** — Insert after the previous component's CSS block
2. **JS element helper** — `{name}El(opts)` returning HTML string
3. **JS render function** — `render{Name}()` returning documentation HTML
4. **Page assembly** — Append `+ render{Name}()` to `main.innerHTML`
5. **NAV array** — Add entry with children for each section ID
6. **sectionIds array** — Add all new `id=` values

### Quality checklist
- [ ] All CSS uses semantic tokens (no raw hex, no `--t1`/`--t2`/`--ctn-*`)
- [ ] All spacing on the global ramp
- [ ] All radius values on the radius ramp (no `5px`/`7px`/`13px`). The ramp's smallest step is `radius-3xs` (4); `radius-2xs` is 6 (companion-chrome tier — kbd badge, Tabs count chip)
- [ ] Any rounded-inside-rounded pair satisfies §2.1.2 nested-radius rule (`inner = outer − inset`); for the canonical 8-radius row with 4-inset that means inner = `radius-3xs` (4)
- [ ] **For every size modifier the component ships, the modifier overrides the FULL tier block — height + radius + font + line-height + icon + gap — not just height.** The §2.3 control-scale table is the source of truth. Setting only some of these creates radius drift the moment a base assumption diverges from the modifier's tier (see §B.36 — Nav S/M and Dropdown / Select panel items all drifted to `radius-2s` (10) because base-class radius cascaded through size modifiers that overrode height but not radius). Audit by side-by-side: render the component's S/M/L next to a Button at the same tier — corner radii should match (24/28 → `radius-xs` 8; 32 → `radius-2s` 10; 40 → `radius-s` 12; 48 → `radius-2m` 14)
- [ ] All `font-size`/`line-height` pairs reference the type ramp tiers (display/label/body × s/m/l + display/2xl)
- [ ] All `box-shadow` recipes for elevation use `--shadow-{1,2,3,4}` tokens (focus halos and active rings excepted)
- [ ] All `z-index` values use `--z-*` tokens
- [ ] Icon glyph size ≠ icon frame size
- [ ] Hover excludes `:focus-within` and `.is-focused`
- [ ] Hover uses real tokens (no `brightness()`)
- [ ] Focus uses two-layer translucent halo
- [ ] All states: default, hover, focus, disabled (+ error/pressed where applicable)
- [ ] Transitions use `.15s ease` or named motion tokens; never `transition: all`
- [ ] Placeholder copy follows convention
- [ ] Icons use verified Phosphor names from §5.3 (Regular weight, `ICON_*` constants only — no raw codepoints, no ad-hoc SVG strings)
- [ ] Optical padding via `:has()`
- [ ] Registered in NAV and sectionIds
- [ ] Field wrapper compatible
- [ ] A11y baseline applied (Part 14): `aria-invalid` on error, `aria-describedby` for caption/validation, `aria-required` on required fields, `aria-haspopup`/`aria-expanded` on triggers that open overlays, `aria-label` on icon-only buttons

