## Part 14 — Accessibility baseline

Every component MUST implement the patterns below. The system already handles the global concerns (`:focus-visible` two-layer halo, Windows High Contrast Mode safety via `outline: 2px solid transparent`, and `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` global override). Component authors are responsible for the per-instance ARIA wiring.

### 14.1 Form field a11y wiring (non-negotiable)
When a control is part of a `ds-field` or `ds-fieldset`, the rendering helper MUST:
1. **Required**: pass `required` attribute on the underlying `<input>`/`<select>`/`<textarea>`. The visible asterisk (`ds-field__required`) keeps `aria-hidden="true"` because the `required` attribute already conveys the requirement to assistive tech.
2. **Invalid**: set `aria-invalid="true"` on the control whenever the field is in an `is-error` state. Without this, screen readers don't know the field is invalid.
3. **Described by**: when a `ds-field__caption` or `ds-fieldset__validation` exists, give it an `id` and reference it from the control via `aria-describedby="<caption-id>"`. This connects the helper/error text to the field for screen readers. If both a caption and a validation message exist, separate IDs with a space: `aria-describedby="cap-id err-id"`.
4. **Labeled**: every control needs either a wrapping `<label>` or an explicit `aria-label`. Selection rows (Checkbox/Radio/Switch row) already wrap their entire row in `<label>` for extended click area — keep that pattern.

### 14.2 Triggers that open overlays
Buttons and trigger surfaces that open an anchored or modal panel MUST carry:
- `aria-haspopup="menu"` (or `"listbox"` / `"dialog"` per role)
- `aria-expanded="true|false"` reflecting open state
- `aria-controls="<panel-id>"` when the panel exists in the DOM

Applies to: Select trigger, future Combobox, Dropdown/ActionMenu trigger, future Disclosure, future Popover trigger.

### 14.3 Icon-only affordances
Any clickable element whose visible content is a single icon MUST have an `aria-label` describing the action ("Close", "Clear", "Toggle visibility", "Open menu", "Sort ascending"). The icon glyph itself is `aria-hidden="true"` so it isn't announced as a separate element. Already applied: `ds-input__action`, `ds-dialog__close`, `chev-btn`.

### 14.4 Live regions (Toast, validation summaries)
- Toast / Snackbar: `role="status"` for advisory, `role="alert"` for errors. Use `aria-live="polite"` for `status` and `aria-live="assertive"` for `alert`. Toasts auto-announce — do not also focus them on appearance (it would steal focus from whatever the user was doing).
- Inline error summary at the top of a form: `role="alert"` + `aria-live="assertive"`.

### 14.5 Modal a11y (Dialog, Drawer)
- `role="dialog"` (default) or `role="alertdialog"` (forced confirmation; cannot be dismissed by clicking the scrim).
- `aria-modal="true"`.
- `aria-labelledby="<title-id>"` referencing the heading; `aria-describedby="<desc-id>"` if a description exists.
- Focus trap inside the modal while open. First focus target is the primary action OR the dialog itself (`tabindex="-1"`). On close, return focus to the trigger.
- ESC key closes (except `alertdialog` which requires explicit user choice).

### 14.6 Keyboard contracts
Each component family has a documented keyboard contract:

| Component | Required keys |
|---|---|
| Button | Space, Enter |
| Checkbox / Radio / Switch | Space (toggle); arrow keys (Radio within group) |
| Input / Textarea / Select trigger | Native focus; Select supports Enter/Space to open, Esc to close |
| Select panel | ↑/↓ to move, Enter to select, Esc to dismiss, Home/End for first/last, type-ahead for prefix matching |
| Tabs | ←/→ to move, Home/End for first/last, Enter to activate (manual mode); roving tabindex |
| Dialog | Tab cycles inside; Esc to close; Shift+Tab reverse |
| Tooltip | Shows on `:focus-visible` of trigger AND on hover; dismisses on blur OR Esc |
| Toast | Tab to focus toast actions; Esc to dismiss focused toast |

### 14.7 Reduced motion
The global `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` rule reduces all transitions/animations to 0.01ms. Components MUST NOT bypass this with `!important` or duplicate transitions. Components whose function depends on motion (e.g., switch thumb position) must use `transform` so the static layout still reads correctly when transitions are disabled.

### 14.8 Color contrast
Every text/background pair must meet WCAG 2.1 AA (4.5:1 for body, 3:1 for large text and graphic icons). The semantic token system is built on a perceptually-uniform OKLCH palette where each shade meets contrast against its paired surface — DO NOT mix tokens across categories (e.g., placing `text/tertiary` on `surface/sunken` is not guaranteed to pass and breaks the contract).
